<title>INDIA: Banks shut in Bombay for local religious festival.</title>
<headline>Banks shut in Bombay for local religious festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>All banks including the Reserve Bank of India were closed in Bombay, India's commercial capital, on Monday for a local religious festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said banks in Madras were also shut. They were open in New Delhi and Calcutta. Bombay and Madras banks reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, the Indian rupee ended at 35.76/77, down from the day's opening quotes of 35.74/76, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
